{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>They gathered a double portion of bread.</b> When they measured what they had gathered in their tents, they found double — two omers for each person. And its midrash: לֶחֶם מִשְׁנֶה — changed: that day it was changed for the better in its fragrance and taste (there)." "<b>And they told Moses.</b> They asked him: how is this day different from the other days? And from this one may learn that Moses had not yet told them the matter of Shabbat that he was commanded to tell them — ״וְהָיָה בַּיּוֹם הַשִּׁשִּׁי וְהֵכִינוּ״ and so on — until they asked ״מַה זֹּאת,״ [and then] he said to them: this is what YHWH spoke [when] I was commanded to tell you. And therefore Scripture punished him [i.e., found fault] in that He said to him ״עַד אָנָה מֵאַנְתֶּם״ — yet did not exclude him from the general [i.e., all-inclusive] statement [addressed to all Israel]."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:45.104212204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}